# FORBIDDEN-TERMS — the project's local list: customer names, products, people, and confidential
# domain terms that must NEVER leave in a report to the upstream framework. One extended regex per
# line (no slashes); empty lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Instantiate it from
# `Maestro/templates/project/FORBIDDEN-TERMS.template` to the project root, named
# FORBIDDEN-TERMS (`Maestro/workflows/W00-project-kickoff.md`, step 4). NEVER send it or paste it
# into an issue: it is read by `bash Maestro/_meta/scan-report.sh <file> FORBIDDEN-TERMS` before
# any report (`Maestro/playbooks/report-framework-improvements.md`) — with hits it exits 1 and
# nothing is sent. Common words get a boundary (\b) so they do not catch substrings; case does not
# matter.
#
# Examples — delete and replace with the project's own:
# \bCustomerName\b
# \bproduct-code-name\b
